  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>x</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>as</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math><br /><br />and <math><mo>-</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></math> has the maximum value <math><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is strictly increasing and hence it is one-one<br /><br />Also,&nbsp;<math><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8734;</mi></mrow></munder><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8734;</mi></math> and <math><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8734;</mi></mrow></munder><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8734;</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Thus, the range of <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is <math><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo></math> hence it is onto.</p>"
